    {
      "id": "r8wsHps1z_X6k-r8ROR46",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1519.1266996106945,
      "y": -4706.614074028204,
      "width": 769.8792724609375,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 27650916,
      "version": 746,
      "versionNonce": 731337308,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781024036034,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "MODULE - I/O Interfacing, Interrupts and DMA\n\nLecture 1: I/O interface, Memory Mapped I/O and Isolated I/O\n\n-> The I/O devices are not connected to system bus directly like Main-Memory\n-> This is because:\n    - Different I/O devices have different data transfer rates\n    - The data transfer rates are irregular in a I/O device\n    - The size of data blocks sent by each I/O device varies significantly\n    - The data format and characteristics of I/O devices vary\n\n-> So each I/O device has an I/O Interface which connects to system bus.\n-> The I/O interface takes care of communication with the cpu",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "MODULE - I/O Interfacing, Interrupts and DMA\n\nLecture 1: I/O interface, Memory Mapped I/O and Isolated I/O\n\n-> The I/O devices are not connected to system bus directly like Main-Memory\n-> This is because:\n    - Different I/O devices have different data transfer rates\n    - The data transfer rates are irregular in a I/O device\n    - The size of data blocks sent by each I/O device varies significantly\n    - The data format and characteristics of I/O devices vary\n\n-> So each I/O device has an I/O Interface which connects to system bus.\n-> The I/O interface takes care of communication with the cpu",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
